{"parentUuid":"d3cf7ed9-b670-459a-871d-bda8043a0549","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BUbtVKdEvKoysht7ajYAp6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QAMFVZeNu8uKpohvQXFfCp","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto","prompt":"Find all memory-related parameters: clause_cleanup_period, clause_cleanup_target, clause_cleanup_ratio, max_clause_activity_value, glucose_decay_increment, share_glue_clauses, share_binary_clauses, max_memory_in_mb, max_size_to_create_precedence_literals_in_disjunctive, presolve_bve_clause_weight, num_search_workers, share_level_zero_bounds. Quote default values and what each does. Also find any \"memory\" or \"size\" cap parameters."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7678,"cache_read_input_tokens":24253,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7678,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosR4HdNXGcqD6SCBXXk","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6657be1e-c091-4267-8e7c-6a3e7dfda298","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:39.643Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d3cf7ed9-b670-459a-871d-bda8043a0549","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017svMiV8N4Jy5jpCa5nM89P","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Memory Leak Analysis\n\nBased on the GitHub issue content provided, here's what can be extracted about the reported memory concern:\n\n## Issue Summary\nThe report documents a memory leak investigation in OR-Tools v9.2's CP-SAT solver on Ubuntu 21.10, identified through Valgrind analysis.\n\n## Diagnosis Method\nThe issue was detected using Valgrind's memory checker with the command `--leak-check=full`, revealing \"1,760 bytes in 5 blocks are possibly lost.\"\n\n## Memory Leak Source\nThe leak originated in the Abseil library's random number generation initialization: \"PoolAlignedAlloc() in pool_urbg.cc:198\" as part of URBG (uniform random bit generator) pool initialization.\n\n## Key Findings\n- **Total heap usage**: 106,898 allocations with 103,952 frees\n- **Possibly lost**: 1,760 bytes in 5 blocks\n- **Still reachable**: 227,963 bytes (likely from logging singletons)\n\n## Notable Observation\nThe issue reporter suspected that \"still reachable\" allocations \"come from some singleton for logging\" and inquired about bypassing the logger to suppress them.\n\n## Resolution Status\nThe issue was assigned to @lperron and targeted for milestone v9.4, but the provided content doesn't include specific fix details, parameter recommendations, or measurements of internal data structure growth."}]},"uuid":"81f0ef64-b3b0-4caa-8af6-79ed75fd2787","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:41.427Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d3cf7ed9-b670-459a-871d-bda8043a0549","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"81f0ef64-b3b0-4caa-8af6-79ed75fd2787","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01BUbtVKdEvKoysht7ajYAp6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YNp4fnRyda9eFkZyXXgdJj","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html","prompt":"Extract details on CP-SAT internal data structures and memory layout: linearization levels, LP relaxation matrix, lazy clause generation overhead, propagator state, domain representation, integer variable encoding (booleans per integer var). What grows with problem size N (number of variables)? Order of magnitude estimates."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7678,"cache_read_input_tokens":24253,"output_tokens":662,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7678},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":662,"cache_read_input_tokens":24253,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7678,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7678,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosR4HdNXGcqD6SCBXXk","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"3a69d8a7-272a-46d2-8f2c-8c60e8c9b099","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:42.282Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6657be1e-c091-4267-8e7c-6a3e7dfda298","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QAMFVZeNu8uKpohvQXFfCp","type":"tool_result","content":"# Memory-Related Parameters in sat_parameters.proto\n\n## Direct Memory Controls\n\n**max_memory_in_mb** (default: 10000)\n- \"Maximum memory allowed for the whole thread containing the solver.\"\n\n## Clause Management Parameters\n\n**clause_cleanup_period** (default: 10000)\n- Determines when cleanup triggers based on learned \"deletable\" clauses accumulated.\n\n**clause_cleanup_target** (default: 0)\n- During cleanup, \"we will always keep that number of 'deletable' clauses.\"\n\n**clause_cleanup_ratio** (default: 0.5)\n- When target is 0, this ratio determines \"the clause_cleanup_ratio of 'deletable' clauses\" deleted.\n\n**clause_cleanup_lbd_bound** (default: 5)\n- \"All the clauses with a LBD lower or equal to this parameters will always be kept.\"\n\n**max_clause_activity_value** (default: 1e20)\n- Scaling parameter for clause activity to prevent overflow.\n\n## Activity Decay Parameters\n\n**glucose_decay_increment** (default: 0.01)\n- Controls variable activity adjustment frequency for search quality.\n\n## Sharing Parameters\n\n**share_binary_clauses** (default: true)\n- \"Allows sharing of new learned binary clause between workers.\"\n\n**share_glue_clauses** (default: true)\n- \"Allows sharing of short glue clauses between workers.\"\n\n## Other Size Constraints\n\n**max_size_to_create_precedence_literals_in_disjunctive** (default: 60)\n- Creates precedence literals only when interval count doesn't exceed this threshold.\n\n**num_search_workers** (default: 0)\n- Parallelism setting affecting memory consumption through multiple solver instances."}]},"uuid":"3348dac2-252a-4fdf-a765-6e203bfbbde3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:44.609Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6657be1e-c091-4267-8e7c-6a3e7dfda298","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3a69d8a7-272a-46d2-8f2c-8c60e8c9b099","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YNp4fnRyda9eFkZyXXgdJj","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Internal Data Structures: Analysis Based on Available Documentation\n\nBased on the provided content, **explicit details about internal data structures and memory layout are not included** in this primer section. The document focuses on algorithmic approaches rather than implementation specifics.\n\n## What the Document Does Cover\n\nThe material describes CP-SAT's operational phases:\n\n**Preprocessing transformations:**\n- \"Domain reduction\" simplifying variable domains\n- \"Expansion of higher-level constraints into lower-level constraints\"\n- Detection of \"affine relations, such as `a * x + b = y`\"\n- Variable probing and substitution operations\n\n**Runtime components mentioned:**\n- Linear relaxations created during the \"Loading and Relaxation\" phase\n- A \"pool of solutions\" maintained during Local Neighborhood Search iterations\n- Multiple solver threads with distinct strategies\n\n## Critical Gap\n\nThe document explicitly states: \"You can find a backup of the old version [here]\" regarding removed introductory content, suggesting technical details were intentionally omitted.\n\n## For Detailed Information\n\nThe primer directs readers to:\n- Source code at GitHub (`ortools/sat` directory)\n- Parameter proto-file documentation\n- Developer talks addressing implementation specifics\n\n**Conclusion:** This educational resource prioritizes conceptual understanding over memory-model analysis. Scaling behavior (Big O with respect to N variables) and encoding overhead specifics require consulting CP-SAT's actual source code or academic papers on Lazy Clause Generation rather than this primer."}]},"uuid":"ceb414c5-ae3a-4cd9-8730-644c0dced9cc","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20: