{"parentUuid":"de15d03a-8faf-4035-93b0-1b5337ee031f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NRgErdA1HG3C97oKuz61VF","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" issue memory model proto large scheduling 70x70 placement grid 200 facilities\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Lanzamientos · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://translate.google.com/translate?u=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fgoogle%2For-tools%2Freleases&hl=es&sl=en&tl=es&client=srp\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/cp_model.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/cp_model.proto\"},{\"title\":\"A memory-based task scheduling algorithm for grid computing based on heterogeneous platform and homogeneous tasks | International Journal of Web and Grid Services\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1504/ijwgs.2020.109473\"},{\"title\":\"Article: A memory-based task scheduling algorithm for grid computing based on heterogeneous platform and homogeneous tasks Journal: International Journal of Web and Grid Services (IJWGS) 2020 Vol.16 No.3 pp.287 - 304 Abstract: Grid computing is a new computing mode in recent years, which focuses on parallel infrastructure and its comprehensive application ability to network computers and distributed processors. Grid computing has been fully applied in the field of modern information technology and computer.\",\"url\":\"https://www.inderscience.com/info/inarticle.php?artid=109473\"},{\"title\":\"Proto | efficient process scheduling library - Community Resources - Developer Forum | Roblox\",\"url\":\"https://devforum.roblox.com/t/proto-efficient-process-scheduling-library/2215440\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Heterogeneous Placeholder Scheduling in Overlay Metacomputers: Early Experiences | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/3-540-36180-4_11\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Heterogeneous Placeholder Scheduling In Overlay Metacomputers: Early Experiences | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/2539672_Practical_Heterogeneous_Placeholder_Scheduling_In_Overlay_Metacomputers_Early_Experiences\"},{\"title\":\"GPU Memory Management for Large Language Models: Optimization Strategies for Production Deployment\",\"url\":\"https://www.runpod.io/articles/guides/gpu-memory-management-for-large-language-models-optimization-strategies-for-production-deployment\"},{\"title\":\"Memory Model Tool\",\"url\":\"https://developer.arm.com/Architectures/Memory%20Model%20Tool\"},{\"title\":\"About OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/introduction\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools and memory-related improvements. OR-Tools includes efforts to reduce memory footprint for large models, and there have been improvements to scheduling cuts and memory management in recent versions.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about a particular issue related to the \"memory model proto\" with \"large scheduling 70x70 placement grid 200 facilities\" that you're asking about. The results show general OR-Tools improvements and documentation, but not this specific issue or test case.\n\nIf you're looking for information about a specific GitHub issue or technical problem with OR-Tools related to this configuration, you might want to:\n1. Check the OR-Tools GitHub repository directly (github.com/google/or-tools)\n2. Search for specific issue numbers if you have them\n3. Look at the OR-Tools issue tracker with more specific keywords\n\nWould you like me to search for more specific information about OR-Tools issues or a particular performance problem you're encountering?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a844208c-cc20-495c-9e17-ceeb200290c3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:08.491Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"de15d03a-8faf-4035-93b0-1b5337ee031f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"adf0da81-b1de-4d7f-95b1-5f4a8673124a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MEDBhr79rsTfAsCRC2WwWb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT log NumConflicts NumClauses memory correlation telemetry\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"ortools cp_solver conflicting constraints · Issue #1398 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1398\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"enable the log of CP-SAT solver · google/or-tools · Discussion #3873\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3873\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-logutils · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpsat-logutils/\"}]\n\nI found some relevant results about CP-SAT. The search returned information about the CP-SAT solver from Google OR-Tools, including references to logging and metrics like NumConflicts. Here are the key findings:\n\nThe CP-SAT solver is designed for integer programming problems and is generally faster than MPSolver. \n\nThe solver has a NumConflicts metric that returns the number of conflicts. \n\nAdditionally, there are resources available for understanding CP-SAT logging: there are utilities for parsing the logs of OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver, and references to educational materials like the CP-SAT Primer that cover understanding the solver's logs and parameters.\n\nThe search results also show there's a GitHub discussion about enabling logging in CP-SAT for large-scale instances, indicating that detailed logging with metrics like NumClauses, memory usage, and correlation telemetry are features that users work with when analyzing solver performance.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5cd20ad5-7f74-45b8-bb14-24d88c114777","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:08.732Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"adf0da81-b1de-4d7f-95b1-5f4a8673124a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a875938e-e219-4230-893b-639e2b6f9d63","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W4uvf76vURsSkAZFQPZBd5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CpSolverResponse\" stats memory ortools log output booleans constraints\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Setting solver limits | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_tasks\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-logutils: Utils for parsing the logs of OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-logutils\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/README.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: com.google.ortools.sat.CpSolver Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/java/classcom_1_1google_1_1ortools_1_1sat_1_1CpSolver.html\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: Google.OrTools.Sat.CpSolverResponse Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/dotnet/classGoogle_1_1OrTools_1_1Sat_1_1CpSolverResponse.html\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: ortools.sat.python.cp_model.CpSolver Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/python/classortools_1_1sat_1_1python_1_1cp__model_1_1CpSolver.html\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"[CP-SAT] Ortools stops when solving a RCPSP - Memory exhausted?\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/d-3P1dq-RBY\"},{\"title\":\"Original CP Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/routing/original_cp_solver\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about `CpSolverResponse` in OR-Tools:\n\n## CpSolverResponse Overview\n\nThe Solve() method returns a CpSolverResponse protobuf that contains the solve status, the values for each variable in the model if solve was successful, and some metrics.\n\n## Key Fields and Statistics\n\nThe solve log will be filled if the parameter log_to_response is set to true.\n\nThe CpSolver returns some statistics on the solution found as a string. Here's an example from the search results showing typical statistics output:\n\nFrom a real example in the logs:\n- `status`: OPTIMAL\n- `objective`: value\n- `best_bound`: value\n- `booleans`: number of boolean variables\n- `conflicts`: number of conflicts detected\n- `branches`: number of branches explored\n- `propagations`: number of propagations\n- `integer_propagations`: integer propagations count\n- `restarts`: number of search restarts\n- `walltime`: elapsed wall clock time\n- `usertime`: user CPU time\n- `deterministic_time`: deterministic time metric\n\n## Response Contents\n\nThe CpSolverResponse contains a feasible solution to the given problem, and depending on the returned status it may be optimal or just feasible. This is in one-to-one correspondence with a CpModelProto::variables repeated field and lists the values of all the variables.\n\nThe response also includes additional information about how the solution was found, and stores model or parameters errors that caused the model to be invalid.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3837ff97-dc45-4653-817c-a5f87220aff2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:13.115Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a875938e-e219-4230-893b-639e2b6f9d63","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
