{"parentUuid":"de6cef2b-18a1-495d-89fb-3f65e2ee0f26","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019UQv5o3eGVT72kwTF8ufHc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0145piUvaMNbBjkc6Z9aaQkq","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html","prompt":"Extract the structure of CP-SAT log output. List the fields available about model size (num_booleans, num_constraints, num_variables, num_integers), search progress (conflicts, branches, propagations, restarts), and any memory-related fields. Also list the per-worker stats fields if shown."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4002,"cache_read_input_tokens":39770,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4002,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":54,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosU9cgxjrUiR71JgDCz","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"5c358daf-ce3e-4405-af6a-e281bd28f837","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:19.522Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5c358daf-ce3e-4405-af6a-e281bd28f837","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019UQv5o3eGVT72kwTF8ufHc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NkFc5Z3haEHoRzmXZSkH2Y","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://www.msoos.org/tag/memory-layout/","prompt":"Extract concrete numbers about SAT solver memory layout: bytes per variable for watched literals, bytes per learned clause, memory layout cost per million variables. Quote any specific measurements or formulas like \"32 bytes per variable\" or \"X bytes per clause of length L\"."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4002,"cache_read_input_tokens":39770,"output_tokens":546,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4002},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":546,"cache_read_input_tokens":39770,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4002,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4002,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosU9cgxjrUiR71JgDCz","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"adc398ee-5018-440e-a527-9b0b6a9b695b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:21.669Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"de6cef2b-18a1-495d-89fb-3f65e2ee0f26","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VsGGpC7r7oUcQAwbenw2Fd","type":"tool_result","content":"# Summary of Issue #2048\n\nBased on the GitHub issue, here are the key details:\n\n## Memory Growth Profile\nThe reporter noted that memory consumption escalated dramatically: \"taking the abs manually needs about 7gb of ram, if I use `AddAbsEquality` instead it goes after finding about 200 solutions (60 Minutes) from 7gb of ram to 32gb of ram without finding any new solution.\"\n\n## Root Cause\nThe issue description does not identify which internal CP-SAT structure caused the problem. The reporter simply observed the problematic behavior without diagnosing the underlying mechanism.\n\n## Resolution\nNo resolution is documented in this issue thread. The issue was created on June 1, 2020, marked as part of milestone v8.0, and assigned to developer lperron, but no follow-up comments or fixes appear in the provided content.\n\n## Diagnostic Metrics\nSpecific measurements regarding RSS, number of variables, constraints, or boolean variables are not provided in the issue report. The reporter only noted they were \"using 7 threads\" and had \"about 50 `AddAbsEqualitys`\" to minimize."}]},"uuid":"4a8524b0-2951-4e31-9396-ebbbb7e95ca2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:24.109Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"de6cef2b-18a1-495d-89fb-3f65e2ee0f26","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5c358daf-ce3e-4405-af6a-e281bd28f837","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0145piUvaMNbBjkc6Z9aaQkq","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Log Structure: Fields and Metrics\n\n## Model Size Fields\n\nThe log reports model dimensions at multiple stages:\n\n- **Variables**: Total count, broken down by type (booleans, integers)\n- **Booleans**: Separate count with domain specifications\n- **Integers**: Count and their domains\n- **Constraints**: Multiple types tracked (`#kLinear1`, `#kLinear2`, `#kLinearN`, etc.)\n\nExample from the document: `\"#Variables: 450 (#bools: 276 #ints: 6 in objective)\"`\n\n## Search Progress Metrics\n\nThe summary section provides cumulative statistics:\n\n- **Conflicts**: Number encountered during search\n- **Branches**: Decision points explored\n- **Propagations**: Total constraint propagations performed\n- **Integer Propagations**: Propagations specific to integer constraints\n- **Restarts**: How many times the search restarted\n\nThe document shows: `\"conflicts: 0 branches: 370 propagations: 13193 integer_propagations: 6897 restarts: 370\"`\n\n## Additional Solution Metrics\n\n- **Walltime**: Elapsed seconds since solver initialization\n- **Deterministic Time**: Normalized time measurement\n- **Gap Integral**: Cumulative optimality gap over time\n- **LP Iterations**: Linear programming solver invocations\n\n## Per-Worker Statistics\n\nThe log includes subsolver timing data showing individual solver contributions, but the document does not detail per-worker breakdown—only aggregate task timing across all workers."}]},"uuid":"51d907b7-9dd9-4097-a452-f582bca074ce","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:24.584Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5c358daf-ce3e-4405-af6a-e281bd28f837","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"adc398ee-5018-440e-a527-9b0b6a9b695b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NkFc5Z3haEHoRzmXZSkH2Y","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Solver Memory Layout Numbers\n\nBased on the blog content, here are the specific measurements provided:\n\n## Watched Literals Memory Cost\n\nThe article states: **\"If the solver uses the typical watched literal scheme, it needs 2 arrays for each variable. If we are using 64b pointers and 32b array sizes, it's 32B for each variable\"**\n\nThis breaks down to **32 bytes per variable** for the watching literal array structure alone.\n\n## Scaling to Large Problems\n\nFor large instances, this creates significant overhead: **\"32MB for every million variable only to keep the watching literal array\"** \n\nThe author illustrates the problem with a concrete example: \"I have seen people complaining that their 100M variable problem runs out of memory — if we count that right that's 3.2GB of memory only to hold the watching literal array pointers and sizes\"\n\n## Clause Storage\n\nWhile the articles discuss memory optimization strategies for binary clauses (using implicit storage and variable-sized watchlist entries), they do not provide explicit formulas for bytes per clause as a function of clause length.\n\n## Cache Impact\n\nThe author notes that cache optimization through variable renumbering **\"can be upwards of 10%\"** in speedup, though this is performance rather than a direct memory measurement."}]},"uuid":"5d17416c-3a17-4a99-a453-b774a0fc81d8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:29.192Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"adc398ee-5018-440e-a527-9b0b6a9b695b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
