{"parentUuid":"3d32f17a-2a90-4a54-9442-365c726c222e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011XSqqyYPVCkjQX9ceZbodd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NisoZDMZWW6Zv3mvJrz3R3","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto","prompt":"Find these specific parameters and quote their default and description: linearization_level, cp_model_presolve, cp_model_probing_level, max_presolve_iterations, presolve_bve_threshold, presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit, share_objective_bounds, share_level_zero_bounds, log_search_progress, log_subsolver_statistics, polish_lp_solution, debug_max_num_presolve_operations, max_domain_size_when_encoding_eq_neq_constraints. Quote literal proto text."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1943,"cache_read_input_tokens":43772,"output_tokens":439,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1943},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":43772,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1943,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosVLRMKvgWHkHUrLbPC","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d195f117-0121-43de-8c17-5f6c8e0b57c8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:38.135Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3d32f17a-2a90-4a54-9442-365c726c222e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KSXA1HDJ3hVd5Cz3yXXxv3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT 2D placement no-overlap diffn memory blowup booleans\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Parameter documentation NoOverlap2D, Cumulative · google/or-tools · Discussion #3107\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3107\"},{\"title\":\"Yet Another Math Programming Consultant: 2d bin packing with Google OR-Tools CP-SAT, how to fix?\",\"url\":\"http://yetanothermathprogrammingconsultant.blogspot.com/2021/02/2d-bin-packing-with-google-or-tools-cp.html\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04B_advanced_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"Placement of products on carrier, layer by layer with CP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/d/topic/or-tools-discuss/T9DUhs2WCao\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT for scheduling Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://schedulingseminar.com/presentations/SchedulingSeminar_LaurentPerron.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Performance of packing problems · google/or-tools · Discussion #3177\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3177\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information related to your query about CP-SAT 2D placement constraints and potential memory/performance issues. Here are the relevant findings:\n\n## Memory and Boolean Variable Issues\n\nAn integer overflow can occur when creating integer variables with very large domains, which relates to the boolean variable blowup you're asking about. In CP-SAT, integers are actually converted to booleans, so large variable domains can create a significant number of internal boolean variables.\n\n## Performance and Propagation Concerns\n\nThe no_overlap_2d propagator is noted to be poor, which directly relates to potential memory issues with 2D placement problems. However, parameters like use_energetic_reasoning_in_no_overlap_2d and use_timetabling_in_no_overlap_2d (formerly use_cumulative_in_no_overlap_2d) have been introduced to improve performance.\n\n## Relevant Constraints\n\nThe add_no_overlap_2d constraint is used to prevent overlaps between intervals on two dimensions, for example for packing rectangles. The issue you're asking about (diffn - the \"different non-overlapping\" constraint) is related to these 2D overlap prevention mechanisms.\n\nThe core issue appears to be that naive implementations of these constraints can generate excessive boolean variables when dealing with large domains or many items, leading to memory blowup. The OR-Tools team has been improving propagation techniques to mitigate this problem.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"44e32ebb-4ef1-4e5e-8861-44243548b6e7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:40.922Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3d32f17a-2a90-4a54-9442-365c726c222e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d195f117-0121-43de-8c17-5f6c8e0b57c8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NisoZDMZWW6Zv3mvJrz3R3","type":"tool_result","content":"# Found Parameters\n\nBased on the provided proto file, here are the parameters you requested:\n\n**linearization_level**: Not found in the visible portion of the file (content ends at line 1000).\n\n**cp_model_presolve**: `optional bool cp_model_presolve = 86 [default = true];`\n\n**cp_model_probing_level**: `optional int32 cp_model_probing_level = 110 [default = 2];`\n\n**max_presolve_iterations**: `optional int32 max_presolve_iterations = 138 [default = 3];`\n\n**presolve_bve_threshold**: `optional int32 presolve_bve_threshold = 54 [default = 500];`\n\n**presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit**: `optional double presolve_probing_deterministic_time_limit = 57 [default = 30.0];`\n\n**share_objective_bounds**: `optional bool share_objective_bounds = 113 [default = true];`\n\n**share_level_zero_bounds**: `optional bool share_level_zero_bounds = 114 [default = true];`\n\n**log_search_progress**: `optional bool log_search_progress = 41 [default = false];`\n\n**log_subsolver_statistics**: `optional bool log_subsolver_statistics = 189 [default = false];`\n\n**polish_lp_solution**: Not found in the visible portion.\n\n**debug_max_num_presolve_operations**: `optional int32 debug_max_num_presolve_operations = 151 [default = 0];`\n\n**max_domain_size_when_encoding_eq_neq_constraints**: Not found in the visible portion."}]},"uuid":"b2de8c8a-8261-4d45-b9ce-78822f37fc1b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:41.389Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d195f117-0121-43de-8c17-5f6c8e0b57c8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e3d5abac-1bbb-4b15-812b-a0c5dfb4d8df","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a08387fbca2c9ad18","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RVwY8JMTyS3eaDt11dPRPg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT lazy clause generation propagator state memory integer variable domain bitmap\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Lazy Clause Generation: Combining the power of SAT and CP (and MIP?) solving\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/lazy.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy Clause Generation: Combining the Power of SAT and CP (and MIP?) Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-13520-0_3\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy Clause Generation: Combining the Power of SAT and CP (and MIP?) Solving\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221353593_Lazy_Clause_Generation_Combining_the_Power_of_SAT_and_CP_and_MIP_Solving\"},{\"title\":\"Propagation via Lazy Clause Generation*\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/COMP90046/resources/lazyj.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy clause generation reengineered Thibaut Feydy and Peter J. Stuckey\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/cp09-lc.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Propagation = Lazy Clause Generation\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/cp07a.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy Clause Generation Reengineered | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-04244-7_29\"},{\"title\":\"Lazy Clause Generation: Combining the best of SAT and CP (and MIP?) solving\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/cpaior-talk.pdf\"}]\n\nI found relevant results about CP-SAT lazy clause generation and propagators. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## CP-SAT Lazy Clause Generation\n\nCP-SAT uses lazy clause generation to combine constraint propagation with SAT solving. The \"lazy\" aspect means clauses are generated on-demand as conflicts are discovered, rather than pre-generating all possible conflict clauses upfront.\n\n## Propagator State and Memory\n\nAfter making a decision, unit propagation is performed to reach a unit propagation fixpoint with assignment A. Every fixed literal is then translated into a domain change, creating a new domain D, and when a propagator finds that f(D) ≠ D the propagator does not directly modify the domain D but instead generates a set of clauses C which explain the domain changes.\n\n## Integer Variable Domain Representation\n\nA domain D is a mapping from a fixed (finite) set of variables V to finite sets of integers. A false domain D is a domain with D(x) = ∅ for some x ∈ V. A domain D1 is stronger than a domain D2, written D1 ⊑ D2, if D1(x) ⊆ D2(x) for all x ∈ V.\n\nThe search results indicate that CP-SAT manages integer variable domains through domain mappings and represents domain states using constraints and literals, but the specific details about bitmap representations for integer variable domains weren't explicitly discussed in these particular sources.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"35c381b5-24b4-4f0a-bc63-c829cc05a7d5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:52:43.201Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e3d5abac-1bbb-4b15-812b-a0c5dfb4d8df","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
